    <string name="sec_keep">Stay alive</string>
    <string name="keep_service">Keep running in background</string>
    <string name="guide_title">Stop Termux from closing</string>
    <string name="guide_intro">Android kills background processes aggressively. Do these steps once; together they fix most random Termux closures.</string>
    <string name="g_battery_title">1. Battery: unrestricted</string>
    <string name="g_battery_body">Exempt both Claude Chat and Termux from battery optimization. On Samsung also add them to Settings → Battery → Background usage limits → Never sleeping apps.</string>
    <string name="g_exempt_self">Exempt Claude Chat</string>
    <string name="g_exempt_done">Claude Chat is exempt</string>
    <string name="g_open_battery">Open battery list (find Termux)</string>
    <string name="g_wake_title">2. Termux wake lock</string>
    <string name="g_wake_body">Holds the CPU awake for Termux. You can also tap \"Acquire wakelock\" in the Termux notification.</string>
    <string name="g_run_wake">Acquire Termux wake lock</string>
    <string name="g_wake_sent">Sent to Termux.</string>
    <string name="g_overlay_title">3. Keep the overlay visible</string>
    <string name="g_overlay_body">An app that is visibly on screen is never treated as cached. Leave the pill, line or curtain overlay on and Termux stays alive.</string>
    <string name="g_phantom_title">4. Phantom process killer (Android 12+)</string>
    <string name="g_phantom_body">The usual cause of sudden closures: Android limits child processes of apps, and proot spawns many. On Android 14+ turn on \"Disable child process restrictions\" in Developer options.</string>
    <string name="g_devopt">Open Developer options</string>
    <string name="g_phantom_adb">Older versions need these commands once over wireless debugging (adb):</string>
    <string name="attach">Attach</string>
    <string name="remove">Remove</string>
    <string name="attach_dir">Attachment folder (inside Ubuntu)</string>
    <string name="attach_note">Attached files are saved to Download/projects on your phone. Claude is given this folder and reads them from there.</string>
